HERE WHAT IS "FLEXBOX" IN THE CSS ??
ans.  "flexbox" is an property which uses the row or the column at one at a time but it helps to under the strongest like if u want to change the direction use the column property of the "flexbox" this is called the "FLEXBOX"
this is my defination to understand the "flexbox" but now lets understand what google is saying
"Flexbox" is a CSS layout system used to arrange elements in one direction (row OR column) with powerful alignment and spacing control.

👉 Think like this:

"Flexbox" = 1-dimensional layout (row or column) it use for the cards layout mainly
uses of the "flexbox"
✅ Align items align "item moves aorund the top to bottom "
✅ Distribute space
✅ Make responsive layouts
✅ Center elements easily
✅ Handle dynamic content size and for the cards

main thing in the "flexbox" how the "flexbox" works in the system let me discribe u in an easy way 
🎯 "Flexbox" Main Concepts

There are 2 axes

1️⃣ "Main Axis" → direction of layout
2️⃣ "Cross Axis" → perpendicular direction

If row →
"Main axis" = horizontal
"Cross axis"= vertical

If column →
"Main axis" = vertical
"Cross axis" = horizontal

there  are the diff types of properties which we use in the flexbox which we learn today 
1 "flex direction" = controls the direction of the item or the container 
=flex-direction: row;
flex-direction: column;
flex-direction: row-reverse;
flex-direction: column-reverse;
this are the 1st type of property we use inn the flex direction we will the example letter

2nd justify content = "justify content moves around the left to right" 
it will align the main element 
here the some property which we use in this section 
justify-content: center;(this means all the item will align in the center )
justify-content: space-between;(this means it align in the center but have space in between them as the name suggest )
justify-content: space-around;(this means it align item in center same as between but the diff is in the edges it gives space in the edges also and between fails to do that )
justify-content: space-evenly ( its an perfect for the evenly spaces in around or the in between it covers edges too...)

3rd flex wrap = { it  controls the wrapping of the container
    "flex-wrap: wrap;
flex-wrap: nowrap;(means all the item contains in the same line may  "shrink" or may  "overflow") (uses of the flex wrap navbar corosiual horizontal menu tabs )
flex-wrap:(👉 Items move to next line when space ends) uses in the "card layout" "product grid" "gallery" "responsive design" 
 "wrap-reverse":(means the same as the flex wrap but in the opposite directions means if normal wrap covers row 1 top row 2 below then the  wrap reverse will happen in this form row 3 bottom and the row 4 above this is called the wrap reverse) "
}

lets understand  the "flex wrap"=is a "Flexbox" container property that controls whether flex items stay in one line or move to the next line when there is not enough space.  



Grid = 2-dimensional layout (row AND column)